;
; Demo Reel 3 through the chipset, with the chipset on screen -- no keyboard.
;
; Runs from the Startup-Sequence, so nothing here may need input.
;
; The USB check comes first and is not decoration. The mouse enumerates
; correctly -- descriptors of 18, 9 and 39 bytes, which is HID -- and then
; never reports anything. The driver's own counters say where the gap is:
; three of them are not per-address, and all three are at zero in every boot
; so far -- no SOF service tick, no parked periodic NAK, no interrupt data --
; so no interrupt IN transfer has ever reached the driver. Nothing below is
; failing; nothing above is asking.
;
; The Startup-Sequence starts the classes like this:
;
;     Run <NIL: >NIL: QUIET AddUSBClasses
;
; asynchronous, quiet, and with its output on NIL:. If that fails it fails
; without telling anyone. So run it here in the foreground with somewhere to
; speak, and print what the stack looks like on either side of it.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel-show] --- USB stack before"
Version >DEBUG: poseidon.library
List >DEBUG: USBCLASSES: LFORMAT "%N"

Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel-show] --- AddUSBClasses, in the foreground"
AddUSBClasses >DEBUG:
Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel-show] --- AddUSBClasses returned"

Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel-show] --- can the guest read what Denise drew?"
DeniseView >DEBUG: NOWINDOW

;
; The overlay covers the whole screen, so a working pointer would be hidden
; under it. It goes up after the USB question has already been answered in
; the log, not before.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel-show] --- putting the aperture on the display"
Run >NIL: <NIL: DeniseView SHOW

;
; toram is a script and Slish is a program; last time both returned at once
; with nothing to show for it, because their output went to the boot console
; and not here. Redirect Execute itself, which carries the commands inside it.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel-show] --- ToRAM (assigns, 1 MB check, tunes to RAM:)"
CD DemoReel3
Execute >DEBUG: toram
Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel-show] --- ToRAM returned"

Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel-show] --- assigns now"
Assign >DEBUG:

Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel-show] --- Slish"
Slish >DEBUG:
Echo >DEBUG: "[demoreel-show] --- Slish returned"
